# Example HTTP requests (httpie-style, curl equivalents in README).

## 1. Daily 09:00 New York with a Monday-weekly alternative

### Daily, DST zone, one extra date and an exception
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/schedules
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "ny-daily-report",
  "timezone": "America/New_York",
  "frequency": "daily",
  "at": "09:00",
  "start_date": "2024-01-01",
  "end_date": "2024-12-31",
  "exceptions": ["2024-07-04"],
  "extra_dates": ["2024-12-26"],
  "ambiguous_policy": "both",
  "gap_policy": "skip",
  "executor": {"type": "log", "payload_template": {"job": "report"}}
}

### Weekly Mon/Wed/Fri 13:45, non-DST zone
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/schedules
{
  "name": "sh-mwf",
  "timezone": "Asia/Shanghai",
  "frequency": "weekly",
  "weekdays": [1, 3, 5],
  "at": "13:45",
  "start_date": "2024-01-01",
  "end_date": "2025-12-31",
  "executor": {"type": "webhook", "url": "http://127.0.0.1:9000/fire"}
}

### Monthly: 1st and last Monday
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/schedules
{
  "name": "monthly",
  "timezone": "Europe/Berlin",
  "frequency": "monthly",
  "nth_weekdays": [{"nth": 1, "weekday": 1}, {"nth": -1, "weekday": 1}],
  "at": "08:30",
  "start_date": "2024-01-01",
  "executor": {"type": "log"}
}

## 2. Inspect materialised fires (stable UTC identities)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8080/schedules/{id}/fires

## 3. Advance the scheduler (deterministic clock hook for demos/tests)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/ticks
X-Test-Now: 2024-11-03T07:00:00+00:00

## 4. Edit a plan -> new version, pending old fires cancelled, history kept
PUT http://127.0.0.1:8080/schedules/{id}
{ ...same body, "at": "10:00"... }

## 5. Pause / resume / delete
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/schedules/{id}/pause
POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/schedules/{id}/resume
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8080/schedules/{id}

## 6. Observability
GET http://127.0.0.1:8080/runs?schedule_id={id}
GET http://127.0.0.1:8080/audit?event=fire.succeeded&limit=50
GET http://127.0.0.1:8080/runtime
